{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a708bfd6-28b5-4e1e-a0fb-a31f0b53be74","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FNqYvbuLnXX8zschfntWEv","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--flashinfer--dsa_sparse_attention_h16_ckv512_kpe64_topk2048_ps64/candidates.jsonl","old_string":"\"reconciled_by\": \"reconcile_ledger.py\"}","new_string":"\"reconciled_by\": \"reconcile_ledger.py\"}\n{\"id\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c002\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T05:20:00Z\", \"source_sha256\": \"8cf8c1ed52233f4524b8b1fb1c53b7dcc68f85a85463dc9879a70d5683e88c4e\", \"design\": \"fused_singlepass\", \"params\": {\"BLOCK_N\": 64, \"num_kv_splits\": 1, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 2, \"pv_dtype\": \"bf16\", \"tokens_per_cta\": 1}, \"hypothesis\": \"H6: c002 (splits=8, 25.45x) and c003 (splits=32, 25.20x) both showed sol_ms FLAT at ~0.128ms independent of split count and num_tokens, falsifying the occupancy hypothesis (H2/H3). The ~0.128ms is fixed per-call overhead = two kernel launches + three fp32 scratch allocs (acc/m/l partials). Removing that overhead via a single fused kernel (one launch, no scratch, no combine) should reduce sol_ms.\", \"prechecks\": {\"lse_formula\": true, \"empty_row_guard\": true, \"splitk_combine\": \"n/a_single_pass\", \"tf32_disabled_where_needed\": true, \"int64_gather\": true, \"smem_budget_ok\": true}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"02d6ae9c64ab42ff93f05c23c53bcb7d\", \"num_tokens\": 8, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 22.429169000241675, \"ref_ms\": 4.336947197914124, \"sol_ms\": 0.19336192071437835, \"max_abs\": 0.015625, \"max_rel\": 19.891929626464844}, {\"uuid\": \"ddfa9e340b264f76abe7418692faa876\", \"num_tokens\": 6, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 19.196448989446722, \"ref_ms\": 3.620259847640991, \"sol_ms\": 0.18859007984399795, \"max_abs\": 0.015625, \"max_rel\": 26.15641212463379}, {\"uuid\": \"9d4a5f21268e484ea05a2f2af91d9fa7\", \"num_tokens\": 2, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 12.979526383940746, \"ref_ms\": 2.2851276707649233, \"sol_ms\": 0.17605632156133652, \"max_abs\": 0.0078125, \"max_rel\": 6.687121868133545}, {\"uuid\": \"f77df5ce21634f7ca0586af7e3c13434\", \"num_tokens\": 2, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 12.967923577593206, \"ref_ms\": 2.2852095770835876, \"sol_ms\": 0.17622016072273256, \"max_abs\": 0.015625, \"max_rel\": 8.577619552612305}, {\"uuid\": \"564007ac354e4662a62cc4d6352dc494\", \"num_tokens\": 8, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 22.32829508868319, \"ref_ms\": 4.281088013648986, \"sol_ms\": 0.1917337618768215, \"max_abs\": 0.0078125, \"max_rel\": 33.8658561706543}], \"all_correct\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 17.450335725326212, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 17.980272607981107, \"decision\": \"reject_regression\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 4, \"skill_usage\": [\"none\"], \"notes\": \"H6 FALSIFIED. Fusing to a single-pass kernel made it SLOWER (geomean 17.45x vs c002 25.45x). sol_ms ROSE to 0.176-0.193ms (from ~0.128ms). So the ~0.128ms floor was NOT launch/scratch overhead; the split-K version was genuinely faster because splitting the 2048-index loop across 8 CTAs hides HBM gather latency better than one CTA serially walking all 2048 indices with a big fp32 acc[16,512] held in registers the whole time. Single-CTA-per-token serializes 32 BLOCK_N iterations and grows the live accumulator's register/latency footprint. CONCLUSION: split-K IS the right structure; the ~0.128ms floor is a real fixed cost (likely the combine launch + a genuine latency floor), not something fusion removes. Revert to split-K family. c002 remains BEST. Next (c005): from c002, reduce the FIXED overhead within split-K by shrinking splits toward the sweet spot AND/OR cutting combine cost -- but since 8->32 splits was flat/slightly worse, try splits=4 (fewer combine reads, larger per-CTA work) to test whether the floor drops. Alternatively vary num_warps/num_stages on c002 to probe the floor.\"}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":77232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5411f58-cf32-4dec-8584-777ec853943a","uuid":"eabb4f90-7b93-4cbf-8ef0-6145774f3146","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:13:10.331Z"}
