h + a genuine latency floor), not something fusion removes. Revert to split-K family. c002 remains BEST. Next (c005): from c002, reduce the FIXED overhead within split-K by shrinking splits toward the sweet spot AND/OR cutting combine cost -- but since 8->32 splits was flat/slightly worse, try splits=4 (fewer combine reads, larger per-CTA work) to test whether the floor drops. Alternatively vary num_warps/num_stages on c002 to probe the floor.\"}","originalFile":"{\"id\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T07:42:11Z\", \"source_sha256\": \"82344276a0443a8d15d82f29983ddcc0d8c9354fd737e50a5dc915ad3cc05964\", \"design\": \"splitK_flashdecode\", \"params\": {\"BLOCK_N\": 64, \"num_kv_splits\": 8, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 2, \"pv_dtype\": \"fp32_ieee\", \"tokens_per_cta\": 1}, \"hypothesis\": \"H1/H2: establish correct split-K flash-decode baseline; expect large win vs fp32-materializing reference\", \"prechecks\": {\"lse_formula\": true, \"empty_row_guard\": true, \"splitk_combine\": true, \"tf32_disabled_where_needed\": true, \"int64_gather\": true}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"02d6ae9c64ab42ff93f05c23c53bcb7d\", \"num_tokens\": 8, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"ddfa9e340b264f76abe7418692faa876\", \"num_tokens\": 6, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"9d4a5f21268e484ea05a2f2af91d9fa7\", \"num_tokens\": 2, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f77df5ce21634f7ca0586af7e3c13434\", \"num_tokens\": 2, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"564007ac354e4662a62cc4d6352dc494\", \"num_tokens\": 8, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"reject_incorrect\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 1, \"skill_usage\": [\"none\"], \"notes\": \"OutOfResources: shared memory Requir